    },
    {
      "id": "11981d854e5899e04dc5843a4b8f59be1782a55e",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 654730889,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> That does not seem correct to me: it's the option length that should be padded to a multiple of 32 bits,\n\nWhat if an option value's length is not a multiple of 32 bits?\n\n[The specification for options in the TLVs in the `LINKTYPE_WIRESHARK_UPPER_PDU` header](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/epan/exported_pdu.h#L54) appears to be modeled after [the specification for options in pcapng files](https://pcapng.github.io/pcapng/draft-tuexen-opsawg-pcapng.html#formatopt).  The latter specification also says that\n\n> Options are a list of Type - Length - Value fields, each one containing a single value:\n> \n> ...\n> \n> Option Length (16 bits): an unsigned value that contains the actual length of the following 'Option Value' field *without the padding octets*.\n\n(emphasis mine).\n\nI.e., in the pcapng spec, \"variable length, padded to 32 bits\" means that the *value* is padded to a multiple of 32 bits; it doesn't mean that the *length value* is rounded up to a multiple of 32 bits.\n\nIf the intent is to work the same way that pcapng options do, then the option length field should *NOT* be rounded up to a multiple of 4 bytes by code that writes options, and code that reads options should treat the length as being the size of the option value, rather than the size of the option value plus padding, and skip the padding to get to the next option.  In addition, the comment that documents the format of the options should copy the text in question from the pcapng spec.\n\nIf the intent is to have the option length field be the length of the option *plus* the length of the padding, then the documentation should explicitly say that *and*, for all options that do *not* have a value length that's a multiple of 4 (such as string options that don't have a multiple of 4 octets in the string, and the DVB event option), indicate how the option is to be interpreted (e.g., for string options, note that, as the padding bytes will be zero, the option string stops either when you run out of length or see a null byte, with the null byte not being part of the value).",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-08-19T07:06:50.973Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-08-19T07:06:50.973Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 112946982,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3895,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0bf1df7a786761fb2d70ebb463bac554ba91a4cd",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 654744930,
          "type": null,
          "body": "If we take as an example the EXP_PDU_TAG_PROTO_NAME, exported-pdu.c is purposely expanding its length to a multiple of 32 bits:\n```\n\t/* Ensure that tag length is a multiple of 4 bytes */\n\tproto_tag_len = ((proto_str_len + 3) & 0xfffffffc);\n```\nI will let Anders comment as he is the initial author, but my understanding was that the padding needed to be included in the length, contrary to pcapng. That's also the assumption of the export_pdu_create_tags() function that assumes the options length is a multiple of 4 bytes:\n```\n\t/* Compute size of items */\n\twhile (*loop_items) {\n\t\ttag_buf_size += (*loop_items)->size_func(pinfo, (*loop_items)->data);\n\t\tloop_items++;\n\t}\n[...]\n\t/* Populate data */\n\tloop_items = items_list;\n\twhile (*loop_items) {\n\t\titem_size = (*loop_items)->populate_data(pinfo, (*loop_items)->data, buffer_data, buf_remaining);\n\t\tbuffer_data += item_size;\n\t\tbuf_remaining -= item_size;\n\t\tloop_items++;\n\t}\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 6722527,
            "username": "pquantin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Pascal Quantin",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9bf49edc6acae0eca821eb90309381794fb4fbea4f3fb7c2378428862ddbb430?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/pquantin"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-08-19T07:22:59.389Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-08-19T07:22:59.389Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 112946982,
