    {
      "id": "36afb7e7d7296f0c874b8962e52ebdf2971c1107",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 655337241,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I think I actually made a mistake with this and in the original bug report. I inadvertently corrupted the packet I was using as an example, which confused me.\n\nBoth the dissector and the exporter are assuming that there is no padding. This means that Wireshark can read the files it produces, and I don't think that there is a bug. The only thing that needs to be changed (I think) is the comment in exported_pdu.h, which currently says that values are padded to 32 bits but should be changed to indicate that no padding is used.\n\nI've attached a corrected version of the output and the hexdump file showing that no padding is produced or expected. Again, these were produced by Wireshark's Import From Hex Dump feature. [corrected_exported.pcapng](/uploads/419f7821e67de8788c32c6e56f6da56b/corrected_exported.pcapng) [corrected_hexdump.txt](/uploads/742b8daf9fc73fc7e4a5c2368ad50a06/corrected_hexdump.txt) I am not sure what the 4-byte alignment is doing in exported-pdu.c, but these files do not appear to use 4-byte alignment.",
          "author": {
            "id": 8145634,
            "username": "danieldulaney",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Daniel Dulaney",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/32640efcc033ecff6416f4f5107edc0777fc37ac83dd005322e8f1d0c9212e69?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/danieldulaney"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-08-19T16:17:58.693Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-08-19T16:17:58.693Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 112946982,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3895,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6cbe9948ea63af2418dd13f8761aa7f1128b64f4",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 655448279,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> The only thing that needs to be changed (I think) is the comment in exported_pdu.h, which currently says that values are padded to 32 bits but should be changed to indicate that no padding is used.\n\nSo are you saying here that a header containing `EXP_PDU_TAG_PROTO_NAME` option with the value \"sip\", and no other options, would, if the fields are big-endian (the spec doesn't appear to say that they are, but the code does), be of the form:\n\n    0x00 0x0a - Option Code = 10, `EXP_PDU_TAG_OPTIONS_LENGTH`;\n    0x00 0x04 - Option Length = 4 bytes;\n    0x00 0x00 0x00 0x13 - Option Value, 19 bytes, that being the total length;\n    0x00 0x0c - Option Code = 12, `EXP_PDU_TAG_PROTO_NAME`;\n    0x00 0x03 - Option Length = 3 bytes;\n    0x73 0x69 0x70 - Option Value, the non NULL-terminated string \"sip\";\n    0x00 0x00 - Option Code = 0, `EXP_PDU_TAG_END_OF_OPT`;\n    0x00 0x00 - Option Length = 0 bytes.\n\n(This also presumes that \"Option Length\" means the length of the option *value*.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-08-19T19:04:28.619Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-08-19T19:04:28.619Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 112946982,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 3895,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "87d1090478e6313967a829f6db98ea4db85dbd2f",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 655495156,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Yes, that looks right to me.\n\nOption 10 is not generated by the importer and is not handled by the decoder. It [falls through the switch statement](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/epan/dissectors/packet-exported_pdu.c#L334) in packet-exported_pdu. However, the rest of it is as expected and produces the correct result. I've attached those bytes loaded into a pcap file for easy viewing: [example_no_length.pcapng](/uploads/5d6a07d565f9d73f767b046a75f8560c/example_no_length.pcapng) [example_with_length.pcapng](/uploads/63ac69e9384ed89bca6e5eed9188e6e7/example_with_length.pcapng)",
          "author": {
            "id": 8145634,
            "username": "danieldulaney",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Daniel Dulaney",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/32640efcc033ecff6416f4f5107edc0777fc37ac83dd005322e8f1d0c9212e69?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/danieldulaney"
          },
